Z||000000||Greg Piet||04-27-2000||03:36 PM||||OK, I think I am just about ready to acquire some autocross tires for racing.<BR>I currently have the turbo rims for my street tires, but now I need to get rims for autocross tires.<BR>Can anybody reccomend rims that would be good and compatable with autocross tires?  I was thinking of the 15 inch rims, but i dont even know if autocross tires come in the right size to mount on those rims.  Also since the rims are for racing and not for show I dont want to waste a perfectly good pair of Fiero rims where somebody else may get a better use for them.  I do however awnt to keep the weight of the rims down.||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-28-2000||08:44 AM||||Rims makes... Panasport, Dymag, Kosei (K1) are all a "superlight" type wheel. oh and Compomotive... all less than 15lbs. as for Tires. what kind of Autocross... Solo I or II. Or IT racing? for parkinglot stomping this will sound strange but the Nitto NT555R (yep DOT Drag tire) has made one GREAT showing on the slalom course. have a high slip angle but not so bad as to be hard to drive. For a fast accurate car get Hoosiers. their pricey and may only last 4 races but you get what you pay for. For a decent DOT tire that you can RAIL on bot on the street and track the Yokohama A032 is a GREAT tire! i have a set of those. LOVE them! they are VERRRRY hard to break loose and have a managable slip angle. Panasports are available at Paul Spruell Afla, Lamorghini, Lotus @ 1-800-522-ALFA. The Kosei are available at <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>  and the Dymag are available at <A HREF="http://www.dymag.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dymag.com</A>  the tires are available at <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tirerack.com</A>    Oh all the tires area available heat cycled and shaved for the ULTIMATE in handeling!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||04-28-2000||10:17 AM||||I have almost new Pirellis on the Grape Ape.  If I ever get it running, I'll let everyone know how well they work.  At least they have a great reputation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||04-28-2000||03:22 PM||||I will be playing in the SOLOII world.  I was thinking of those Hoosiers which are called autocross tires.  The rims you have described sound more expensive than the rest of my car.  I was trying to avoid something heavy like steel rims.<P>I currently am running stock turbo rims and a set of YokoHamas (s300 or something), so any type of sticky tire would work well.<BR>At the races people seem to love Kuhmo's but I dont know squat about these fancy fancy tires.||||reg||1
